# Project baseline

This is a modular monolith. Keep one API, one PostgreSQL database, and one Redis instance.

- Put business behavior in `apps/api/src/modules` only when a phase asks for it.
- Keep infrastructure in `apps/api/src/platform`.
- The backend is authoritative. `packages/api-contracts` holds shared request and response types only.
- Use tenant terminology. Do not add a `customers` table beside tenants.
- Do not add microservices, Kafka, RabbitMQ, a service mesh, or an API gateway unless a later task asks.
- Do not put `googleId` or `appleId` on users.
- Do not put password hashes on the `users` table.
- Do not hardcode campaign, payment, AI, analytics, marketplace, or vegetarian-specific domain types in the foundation.

```text
apps/api/src/
├── config/
├── bootstrap/
├── modules/
├── platform/
└── shared/
```
